% ══ COLUMN 3 ══
\posterbox[bluecard, title={A Framework for Responsible Deployment}]
{name=framework, column=3, between=row5 and row15}{
  \fontsize{34}{44}\selectfont
  The path to safe clinical integration requires a rigorous, multi-stakeholder governance structure:
  \vspace{24pt}

  \begin{enumerate}[label={\color{secondary}\bfseries Phase \arabic*.}, itemsep=20pt]
    \item \textbf{Rigorous Prospective Evaluation:} Move beyond multiple-choice benchmarks to test models in diverse, real-world clinical settings before full deployment.
    \item \textbf{Human-in-the-Loop Design:} Maintain mandatory clinician oversight of all LLM-generated diagnostic and therapeutic outputs.
    \item \textbf{Transparent Reporting:} Standardize the disclosure of model limitations, training data sources, and known failure modes to clinicians.
    \item \textbf{Continuous Equity Audits:} Actively monitor and assess differential performance or bias across patient demographics.
    \item \textbf{Regulatory Alignment:} Sync deployments with evolving guidance from the FDA, EMA, and WHO on AI-based medical devices.
  \end{enumerate}
}

\posterbox[highlightcard, title={Key Takeaways}]
{name=takeaways, column=3, between=row15 and bottom}{
  \fontsize{36}{46}\selectfont\color{white}
